  "progression": "The Compas example for September 2026 entrants includes 60 EC in each year. The major includes 156 EC, with a 6 EC bachelor thesis. The first-listed 24 EC faculty minor is Amsterdam Global Health, subject to selection, capacity and future offering. The extra thesis in the 30 EC version for visiting students does not enter the ledger. Year two requires the binding study advice threshold of 42 first-year EC. Year three requires all of year one and 30 EC in year two. Minor entry additionally requires 18 EC from semester 2.1. The care placement requires preparation or equivalent skills accepted by its examiner. GP placement requires satisfactory professional behavior in the care placement and examiner approval. Patient-related teaching requires confidentiality and participation. The Dutch language test or remedial work gates Doctor and Patient 1. Clinical, progress and portfolio assessments and research introductions are embedded. The bachelor thesis normally follows the minor and uses a short systematic review or an eligible report of research-minor work. It is supervised and written individually in scientific English. The current registration deadlines apply to the current third-year cohort. VUMED360 starts in September 2027. Compas regular teaching ends after 2028–2029, and the last graduation date is 31 August 2030. Compas credits do not transfer into VUMED360.",
  "minorSelection": "First listed published 24 EC faculty minor as a bounded example. Current Amsterdam Global Health includes participatory research, health inequalities, primary and community care and diversity. The optional extra minor thesis for visiting non-Medicine students is excluded.",
